# SFT execution status v0.110

2026-09-23. The full-size input/output layout adapter is implemented and locally
tested. **Gate 5 remains incomplete and execution stays closed.** No native
layout, checkpoint/tokenizer payload read, S3 request, GPU operation or training
occurred. All five new files remain local and unpushed.

## Completed this step

The new private adapter accepts separately acquired checkpoint/tokenizer siblings
without copying, hashing or changing permissions on either input. Supplied
source/control bindings and exact plan inventory sizes are validated first.
Two metadata-only tree passes reject changed identities, aliases, unexpected
entries and wrong ownership/mode/size/link count.

Before any mutation it reserves the combined source/target node and content
capacity. It creates four tracked empty rootfs mount targets and two fresh
output/mountpoint siblings, then invokes the unchanged source/control addon,
which freezes the owned root. Final private mount controls bind post-creation
parent metadata, the prepared root and targets, and pinned input/output roots.
Started failures taint and retain the partial attempt; there is no retry or
cleanup. Public `prepare_layout` always rejects with `host_guard_not_bound`.

This completes the local adapter, not input acquisition/authentication,
immutable backing or external-writer exclusion. Returned paths and identity
maps remain private; only the aggregate receipt is suitable for retention.
The existing source-addon content cap remains 5,191,700 bytes and excludes
filesystem metadata, OS overhead and separate acquisition/import work.

## Verification

**521 unique tests pass on CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7**, with zero errors,
failures or skips: 30 new tests and 491 prior regressions. The actual metadata
walk/listing helpers execute against in-memory syscall doubles; input files
have metadata only, with no payload bytes allocated or read.

Independent review found and resolved an empty-list versus empty-set mismatch
that would have rejected successful layouts after freeze. Final review found
no remaining substantive source/test defect or accidental native call. Tests
check leaked descriptors after every rejection path and reject reuse after
started failures. Final root follow-up strengthened late-close testing and
reran the entire suite on both runtimes.

Syntax/AST, 100-column and trailing-whitespace checks pass. Ruff was not rerun:
the previous temporary executable is gone, and no replacement was downloaded.
All 44 prior development/readiness bindings, 78 qualified native source rows
and 39 worker source rows still match. Earlier evidence and manifests are
unchanged; tracked and staged diffs remain empty.

